Subject: [PATCH 6.12.y 0/2] Bluetooth: L2CAP: fix the deferred ECRED accept hang

Hello,

this is a backport to 6.12.y of two mainline commits by Pauli Virtanen,
in this order:

  608e0b7a675b ("Bluetooth: L2CAP: add l2cap_chan_close_unlocked() and
  locking helpers")
  32d86e048d8e ("Bluetooth: L2CAP: hold conn->lock for
  __l2cap_ecred_conn_rsp_defer")

The second fixes ab4eedb790ca ("Bluetooth: L2CAP: Fix corrupted list in
hci_chan_del"), which 6.12.y has as f87271d21dd4; it needs the first
for l2cap_chan_lock_conn() and l2cap_chan_unlock_conn(). Neither
carries Cc: stable. They are patches 2 and 7 of the series "Bluetooth:
L2CAP: fix and annotate l2cap_conn::chan_l locking"; the other patches
are not needed for the problem below and were not tested here.

Without them, BlueZ's l2cap-tester case "L2CAP Ext-Flowctl Server -
Accept 2 Close 1" never finishes on v6.12.114: the test stops after
"Accept deferred setup". (On v7.3 the hung-task detector shows the
tester's task holding its socket's lock from l2cap_sock_recvmsg() and
waiting for the same lock in l2cap_sock_teardown_cb(); patch 2
releases the socket lock before __l2cap_ecred_conn_rsp_defer().)

On 6.12.y patch 1 does not build and patch 2 does not apply as they
are. Deviations:
- patch 1: the context-analysis annotations 6.12.y lacks are dropped
  (__must_not_hold, the __cond_acquires on l2cap_chan_lock_conn(),
  __context_unsafe); the code is unchanged;
- patch 2: l2cap_sock_recvmsg() in 6.12.y has no MSG_ERRQUEUE block,
  so the three MSG_ERRQUEUE lines that precede the new
  l2cap_sock_defer() call upstream are absent; l2cap_sock_defer() and
  its call are as upstream.

Tested on v6.12.114 in QEMU/KVM (4 vCPUs) with BlueZ's
doc/tester.config: with the series the case passes, and the whole
l2cap-tester ends with 33 of 111 passed; each of the 78 failing cases
also fails on plain v6.12.114. Without the series the case never
finishes. No lockdep or KASAN report in either. The low total is
mostly an unrelated 6.12.y defect, every L2CAP getsockopt() failing
with EOPNOTSUPP on v6.12.114, which 5bd0dec150f5 ("net: call
getsockopt_iter if available"), already queued for 6.12, fixes.

The two commits are requested for 7.3.y and 7.2.y as they are, in a
separate mail; backports for 6.18.y and 6.6.y are separate series.

Thanks,
Iaroslav

